+<BR>
+Class Utf8Decoder</H2>
+<PRE>
+<A HREF="http://docs.oracle.com/javase/6/docs/api/java/lang/Object.html?is-external=true" title="class or interface in java.lang">java.lang.Object</A>
+  <IMG SRC="../../../../resources/inherit.gif" ALT="extended by "><A HREF="http://docs.oracle.com/javase/6/docs/api/java/nio/charset/CharsetDecoder.html?is-external=true" title="class or interface in java.nio.charset">java.nio.charset.CharsetDecoder</A>
+      <IMG SRC="../../../../resources/inherit.gif" ALT="extended by "><B>org.apache.catalina.websocket.Utf8Decoder</B>
+</PRE>
+<HR>
+<DL>
+<DT><PRE>public class <B>Utf8Decoder</B><DT>extends <A HREF="http://docs.oracle.com/javase/6/docs/api/java/nio/charset/CharsetDecoder.html?is-external=true" title="class or interface in java.nio.charset">CharsetDecoder</A></DL>
+</PRE>
+
+<P>
+Decodes bytes to UTF-8. Extracted from Apache Harmony and modified to reject
+ code points from U+D800 to U+DFFF as per RFC3629. The standard Java decoder
+ does not reject these.
+<P>
+
+<P>
