             Bug #: 53050
           Summary: org.apache.catalina.session.ManagerBase has issues
                    with update the seed (initialized to
                    System.currentTimeMillis()), since only the 32 least
                    significant bits are changed by the XOR.
           Product: Tomcat 6
           Version: 6.0.24
          Platform: PC
        OS/Version: Windows Vista
            Status: NEW
          Severity: normal
          Priority: P2
         Component: Catalina
        AssignedTo: dev@tomcat.apache.org
        ReportedBy: andras_rozsa@yahoo.com
    Classification: Unclassified


Line 563: long seed = System.currentTimeMillis();
...
Line 567: long update = ((byte) entropy[i]) << ((i % 8) * 8);
Line 568: seed ^= update;

The byte-cast in Line 567 should be replaced by a long-cast.

With the byte-cast of entropy[i] the long update becomes a 32-bit int, so the
32 most significant bits of the seed will not be updated by the XOR in Line
568.

