=0A> If a file named index.jsp is declared as a welcome and it is not there=
 in the system, tomcat does not allow failover to framework like Tapestry.=
=0A=0AIt sounds like behaviour that can be controlled by=0A"resourceOnlySer=
vlets" option in <Context>,=0ASee=0Ahttp://tomcat.apache.org/tomcat-7.0-doc=
/config/context.html=0A=0AThe current behaviour is caused by compatibility =
concerns with earlier=0Aversions of Tomcat. Read the doc for more details.=
=0A=0A=0A> =A0However, if a file named=A0Bienvenue.jsp is declared as welco=
me file, the failover is allowed.=0A=0AUnlikely. You have to provide specif=
ic example to confirm that. The=0Aabove mentioned option could explain that=
 as well.=0A=0A> However=A0 =A0  <welcome-file-list />=0A> is ignored and s=
erver picks up default values in ${Tomcat.home}/conf/web.xml=0A=0Aconf/web.=
xml is not just default. It is merged with app's web.xml=0Ausing the rules =
for merging web fragments, as specified in the Servlet=0A3.0 Rev.a specific=
ation.=A0 If current behaviour contradicts with=0Aspecification, please cit=
e what point in merging algorithm is not=0Afollowed.=0A=0ABest regards,=0AK=
