>>=20
>> as the spec dictates every jsp file that specify session=3D"true"  =
(this is default in tomcat  )  forces a new session to be created, =
wether or not we are using the session inside the jsp file.
>>=20
>> the session is triggered for creation at PageContextImpl file, isn't =
meaningfull  to make this session creation on demand ?
>=20
> It is not possible, because (by specification) the JSP page (unless it
> has session=3D"false")  needs to have local variable named "session"
> that can be used from
> java fragments (aka scriptlets).
>=20
> You cannot create a Java variable "on demand".
>=20
> Note that there is "needsSession" attribute in
> PageContextImpl#_initialize(..), which is not always true.
>=20
>=20
>> Most of the jsp files are using the session for checking an attribute =
presence, so creating a new session just for get operations  is a wast =
of memory.
>> do I miss something ? I am ready to do the development, maybe someone =
is working on this already ?
>=20
>=20
> Best regards,
> Konstantin Kolinko
